{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2DimTranspose","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2DimTranspose","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2ContentTranspose"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.dimHLF_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.dimHLF_conj","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2DimTranspose.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**C2 capstone (`q = 1`): the SYT dimension is transpose-invariant**, `f^λ = f^{λ'}`.\n`dimHLF λ = |λ|! / ∏_c h_c`; both `|λ|` (`sz_conj`) and `∏_c h_c` (`prodHooks_conj`) are\ntranspose-invariant, so the Frame–Robinson–Thrall dimension is too.  This is the `q = 1`\nspecialisation of the keystone weight symmetry `W_λ = W_{λ'}` (necessary condition C2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sz_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sz_conj","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2DimTranspose.lean#L83-L85","doc":"**Size is transpose-invariant**: `|λ'| = |λ|` — both count the cells (`Σ_j colLen l j = Σ_i λ_i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.prodHooks_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.prodHooks_conj","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2DimTranspose.lean#L62-L81","doc":"**The hook-length product is transpose-invariant**: `∏_c h_c (λ') = ∏_c h_c (λ)`.  Product analog\nof `sumSqHooks_conj`: the conjugate's hook at `(r,c)` equals `l`'s hook at `(c,r)` (commute arm/leg\nvia `colLen_conj`), and `cell_fubini_prod` matches the cell sets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cell_fubini_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.cell_fubini_prod","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2DimTranspose.lean#L47-L60","doc":"**Product cell-Fubini** (product analog of `cell_fubini`): a row-indexed cell product equals the\ncolumn-indexed one, via the column-length duality `colLen_duality`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.list_range_map_sum_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.list_range_map_sum_gen","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2DimTranspose.lean#L37-L45","doc":"List→Finset **sum** bridge over a general `AddCommMonoid` (the file's `list_range_map_sum` is\n`ℤ`-only; `sz_conj` below needs the `ℕ` instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.list_range_map_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.list_range_map_prod","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2DimTranspose.lean#L28-L35","doc":"List→Finset **product** bridge (product analog of `list_range_map_sum`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}